From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: turn off the AIC8801 firmware's 5 GHz link detection

With link_det_5g set (the firmware image default), the firmware keeps a table
of 5 GHz access points it joined with VHT or HE. A second join to the same
BSSID before a link check passed (at least 50 received data frames in a 30 s
window, at most half of them retries) is made with HT only, and nothing clears
the entry for the rest of the firmware run, so the link stays Wi-Fi 4 until
the chip is restarted. The test is made at the join, so a deauthentication
and reconnect soon after the first association (for example while
wpa_supplicant settles) is enough to keep a 5 GHz link at HT.

The vendor build sets CONFIG_LINK_DET_5G = y, which leaves the boot patch
entry {0x104 link_det_5g = 0} out of patch_tbl. Build without it.

The firmware applies boot patch entries when it starts, after its .data is
initialised. Reloading the modules does not restart a running chip, so the
change takes effect at the next power-on of the chip (a reboot).
---
--- a/aic8800_bsp/Makefile
+++ b/aic8800_bsp/Makefile
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 CONFIG_GPIO_WAKEUP ?= n
 CONFIG_M2D_OTA_AUTO_SUPPORT = n
 CONFIG_M2D_OTA_LZMA_SUPPORT = n
-CONFIG_LINK_DET_5G = y
+CONFIG_LINK_DET_5G = n
 CONFIG_MCU_MESSAGE = n
 CONFIG_FIRMWARE_ARRAY = n
 # Need to set fw path in BOARD_KERNEL_CMDLINE
